WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.280
After what feels like forever, Daniel Craig's&nbsp;
swan song as British secret agent James Bond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.480
is approaching. Here's everything we know&nbsp;
about No Time to Die, the 25th Bond film.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.280
"No Time to Die" was originally scheduled for&nbsp;
release in November 2019, but when original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.800
director Danny Boyle dropped out due to creative&nbsp;
differences, it was pushed back twice. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:27.360
COVID-19 arrived, and "No Time to Die" was delayed&nbsp;
to April 2021 — becoming the first tentpole movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:33.200
from a major franchise to be delayed due to&nbsp;
COVID-19. Finally, Universal pushed "No Time to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.560
Die" back once again to October 8, betting that&nbsp;
more movie theaters will be open in the fall.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.720
"No Time to Die'' has a big cast with many&nbsp;
returning characters along with some exciting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.480
new additions. Many 007 franchise mainstays&nbsp;
will be back, including Ralph Fiennes as M;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.920
Ben Whishaw as Q; Naomie Harris as&nbsp;
Moneypenny; Rory Kinnear as Tanner;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:00.560
Jeffrey Wright as CIA Agent Felix Leiter; and&nbsp;
Léa Seydoux as MI6 psychiatrist Madeleine Swann.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.120
Christoph Waltz will also be reprising&nbsp;
his role as villain Ernst Stavro Blofeld,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.040
who was captured at the end of&nbsp;
"Spectre" and is now in MI6 custody.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.240
Newcomers include "Bohemian&nbsp;
Rhapsody" star Rami Malek,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.400
who will be playing the villain of "No&nbsp;
Time to Die," the aptly named Lyutsifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.480
Safin. Lashana Lynch will play Nomi, a new 00&nbsp;
agent who joined MI6 after Bond's retirement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.840
and Ana de Armas will play Paloma, a CIA&nbsp;
agent who teams up with Bond to battle Safin.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.080
Those behind the camera are just as important&nbsp;
as those in front of it when it comes to film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:38.000
and television projects. Cary Joji Fukunaga — the&nbsp;
genius behind "True Detective" Season 1 — directed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.960
"No Time to Die." This marks the first Bond film&nbsp;
for the director, for which he also co-wrote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.000
the screenplay alongside Neal Purvis, Robert&nbsp;
Wade, and "Fleabag's" Phoebe Waller-Bridge.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.520
Purvis and Wade worked together on the&nbsp;
screenplays for "The World is Not Enough,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.520
"Die Another Day," "Casino Royale,"&nbsp;
"Quantum of Solace," "Skyfall," and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.040
"Spectre." It would have been shocking&nbsp;
not to see their names on the credits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.892
and thankfully they were fully on board&nbsp;
to write Daniel Craig's last film as 007.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.360
The film is also executive produced&nbsp;
by Chris Brigham, who boasts works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.400
like "Inception" and "Argo." You also can't&nbsp;
have Bond without producer Barbara Broccoli,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.280
who's second credit ever was "License to Kill,"&nbsp;
and has worked on every Bond production since. 

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:18.400
"The past isn't dead"

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.680
The trailer gives us a few hints of what to&nbsp;
expect from the movie. Years after the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.600
of "Spectre," a retired 007 is recruited by his&nbsp;
old ally Felix Leiter for one more mission. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.560
Bond discovers that a man named Safin is behind&nbsp;
a plot that could kill millions of people. As for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.440
what Safin's supervillain scheme is specifically,&nbsp;
we'll have to wait until October to find out.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.600
In terms of themes, Fukunaga believes that&nbsp;
"No Time to Die" is "the culmination of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.080
Bond has become." Daniel Craig's James Bond has&nbsp;
been through a lot, from the death of his lover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.480
in "Casino Royale" to the destruction of his&nbsp;
childhood home in "Skyfall." It appears that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.200
Craig's final chapter as Bond will see the&nbsp;
character confronting his many, many demons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.840
and possibly getting something like closure&nbsp;
— until the next Bond comes along, anyway.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.400
"This will be the final chapter for Daniel Crag" 

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.520
The Daniel Craig-led 007 films are widely popular&nbsp;
for their theme songs, which always manage to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.400
capture each movie's overall tone. Adele's&nbsp;
"Skyfall" theme was an Academy Award winner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.040
and Sam Smith also nabbed an Oscar for his&nbsp;
"Spectre" theme song, "Writing's On the Wall."

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.960
It's no surprise that "No Time to Die" will&nbsp;
feature a theme song by one of the decade's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.520
most prominent artists — Billie Eilish. The&nbsp;
young singer provides the vocals for the song,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:31.680
also titled "No Time to Die." The&nbsp;
track was released in October 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.040
putting its debut and the&nbsp;
film's almost one year apart.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.960
Additionally, the great Hans Zimmer serves&nbsp;
as the composer of "No Time to Die,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.000
marking the legendary musician's&nbsp;
first work on a Bond film.

